          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category"} higher category
            is called
            %em van Kampen
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#SobocinskiHeindel11"}> Sobocinski &amp; Heindel 2011
            \&amp;rbrack; if it is both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimit"} universal
            (i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback-stability"} stable
            under
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exactness+properties"} exactness properties
            can be phrased in terms of certain colimits being van Kampen.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
          #eq:SelfIndexingFunctor.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S
                  \\,\colon\,
                  \\mathcal{C}^{op} \to Cat
          %p
            defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(x) \,\coloneqq\, \mathcal{C}/x
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-indexing"} self-indexing
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
          %p
          #VanKampenColimit.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is
              %strong van Kampen
              if it is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserved
              by the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SelfIndexingFunctor"} (1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %h3#universality_and_descent Universality and descent
          %p We need the following notation:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo ▿
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}^{\triangledown}
                for the result of adjoining to it a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                inclusion
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo ▿
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{D}^{\triangledown}
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \,\colon\, \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}
                a
                = succeed "-shaped" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mi G
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim} G \,\in\, \mathcal{C}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi G
                        %mo ▿
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo ▿
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^{\triangledown} \,\colon\, \mathcal{D}^{\triangledown} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
                the extension of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo ▿
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}^{\triangledown}
                by assigning
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim} G
                to the adjoined terminal object.
          %p
          #UniversalityAndDescent.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (equifibrancy characterization of van Kampen colimits)
              %br/
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              has all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              of
              = succeed "-shaped" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}G
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \colon \mathcal{D}\to \mathcal{C}
              is van Kampen (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VanKampenColimit"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  For any diagram
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mo ▿
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒟
                          %mo ▿
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{\triangledown} \,\colon\, \mathcal{D}^{\triangledown} \to \mathcal{C}
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi α
                          %mo ▿
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mo ▿
                        %mo ⇒
                        %msup
                          %mi G
                          %mo ▿
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^{\triangledown} \,\colon\, F^{\triangledown} \Rightarrow G^{\triangledown}
                  whose
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restriction
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon F \Rightarrow G
                  along
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo ↪
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒟
                          %mo ▿
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{D}^{\triangledown}
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equifibered+natural+transformation"} equifibered
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi α
                              %mo ▿
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^{\triangledown}
                      is
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equifibered+natural+transformation"} equifibered
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi F
                              %mo ▿
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{\triangledown}
                      is a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimiting
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              First note that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\circ G
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⇓
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big([\mathcal{D},\mathcal{C}] \Downarrow G\big)
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    [\mathcal{D},\mathcal{C}]/G
            %p
              consisting of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equifibered+natural+transformation"} equifibered transformations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi lim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(x) \to \lim (S\circ G)
              is identified with the pullback functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⇓
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}/x \longrightarrow ([\mathcal{D},\mathcal{C}] \Downarrow G)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now, this functor has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              given by taking
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#FullyFaithfulAndInvertibleAdjoints"} Therefore
              it is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
              if and only if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
              of the adjunction are isomorphisms.
            %p
              The unit is the map from an equifibered transformation over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              into the pullback of its colimit. The latter underlies an equifibered
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha'
              by construction, so the unit is an isomorphism just when
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mtext (2)
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mtext (1)
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{(2)}\Rightarrow \text{(1)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              from the colimit of its pullback. Thus, it is an isomorphism just when
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mtext (1)
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mtext (2)
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{(1)}\Rightarrow\text{(2)}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The condition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtext (1)
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mtext (2)
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{(1)}\Rightarrow\text{(2)}
              is precisely the statement that the colimit of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimit"} universal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtext (2)
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mtext (1)
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{(2)}\Rightarrow\text{(1)}
              is a form of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
          %h3#colimits_in_span Colimits in Span
          #ColimitsInSpan.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A colimit in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is van Kampen if and only if it is preserved by the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Span
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Span(C)
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spans"} spans
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#SobocinskiHeindel11"}> Sobocinski &amp; Heindel 2011
            ).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  A category with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lextensive+category"} lextensive
                  just when
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  are van Kampen.
              %li
                %p
                  A category with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adhesive+category"} adhesive
                  just when
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
                  are van Kampen.
              %li
                %p
                  A category with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exhaustive+category"} exhaustive
                  just when transfinite
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
                  of monomorphisms are van Kampen.
            %p
          %p
          #RegularCatWithVanKampColimitsIsExact.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
              with van Kampen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruences"} congruences
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1, p_2 : R \rightrightarrows A
              be a congruence. We need to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+map"} quotient map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to A/R
            %p
              Let the transitivity of the congruence be witnessed by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi A
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \,\colon\, R \times_A R \to R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi A
                            %mi R
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⇉
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi π
                                  %mn 2
                              %mi t
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi π
                                      %mn 1
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⇉
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 2
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    R \times_A R
                    \&amp;
                    \\underoverset{\pi_2}{t}{\rightrightarrows}
                    \&amp;
                    R &amp; \stackrel{p_2}{\to} &amp; A
                    \\\
                    {{}^\mathllap{\pi_1}}\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow{{}^\mathrlap{p_1}} &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    R &amp; \underoverset{p_2}{p_1}{\rightrightarrows} &amp; A &amp; \to &amp; A/R
                    }
            %p
              the left squares are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              and the top diagram is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+coequalizer"} split coequalizer
              (with the splitting maps given by reflexivity),
              %a{:href => "split+coequalizer#AsCoequalizers"} hence
              a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalityAndDescent"}
              implies that also the right square is a pullback. But this is the desired statement that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to A/R
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    2 &amp; \to &amp; 1
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    1 &amp; \to &amp; 1
                    }
            %p
              is not van Kampen, neither is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
              diagram
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf 1 \rightrightarrows \mathbf 1 \to \mathbf 1
            %p
              On the other hand, in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              (say
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
              seen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+type#types_equivalent_to_the_circle_type"} as a coequalizer
              gives a concise proof that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
              of the circle is equivalent to the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{id}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              are isomorphisms, and the top row is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coequalizer"} homotopy coequalizer
              diagram because the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+type"} line type
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent"} homotopy coherent
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⇉
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇉
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}
                    \&amp;
                    \\underoverset{\mathrm{id}}{s}{\rightrightarrows}
                    \&amp;
                    \\mathbb{Z} &amp; \to &amp; \mathbf{1}
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{1} &amp; \rightrightarrows &amp; \mathbf{1} &amp; \to &amp; S^1
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    }
            %p
              Then, descent implies that the square on the right is a pullback, which says exactly that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"} path space
              between any two points of the circle is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %h2#InHigherCategories In higher categories
          %p
            There is an evident generalization of the definition to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
          %ul
            %li
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              just when
              %em all
              colimits are van Kampen.
          %p
            If we take Theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalityAndDescent"}
            as the definition of “van Kampen colimit”, this follows from Theorem 6.1.3.9 of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HTT"} HTT
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C2%29-Categories+and+the+Goodwillie+Calculus"} Lurie 2Cats+Goodwillie, example 1.2.3
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalityAndDescent"}
            may not exactly be in the literature, however. The cited theorem of HTT essentially gives Theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalityAndDescent"}
            under the additional global hypothesis that all colimits in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are universal.
          %p
            In this case, being van Kampen is also equivalent to being preserved by the composite of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Core
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Core : (\infty,1)Cat \to \infty Gpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            (specifically, the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor+theorem"} representable functor theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Core
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Core \circ S
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifiers"} object classifiers
            exist.
